I won a game on 3.07.  I played as a wizard, and started out
with a spellbook of create monster, and a ring of conflict.
I got myself up to level 7, while still on the first level,
then went downstairs.  I found a lawful altar on the second
level, dipped some useless potions in fountains and made
holy water on the altar. Using one I blessed the spellbook
(#dip'ed it in holy water).  Going further down, I found
another altar on level 8 (I wanted to keep the lawful altar),
and stayed there for about a week, real time, creating monsters
and sacrificing.  Finally one came along with a wand of polymorph
and all the junk that the monsters had been dropping came in
handy.  I gathered all the junk from above me, and down to
about level 16, cleaned out about 3 shops, then started
polymorphing. Finally got a wand of wishing, wished for 3 cursed
scrolls of genocide, genocided minotaurs, and wound up with
about 15 wands of digging, two more wishes and I had ~35 wands
piled up on top of the other stuff.  When I finally left to
get the Amulet, I had (just the important stuff):
	3 blessed amulets of life saving
	+6 blessed war-hammer named Mjollnir (rust proofed)
	+5 blessed athame (rust proofed)
	+6 blessed long sword named Excalibur
	+6 blessed gray dragon scale mail
	+6 blessed cloak of protection
	+5 blessed Hawiian shirt
	+5 blessed gauntlets of power (rust proofed)
	+6 blessed shield of reflection (rust proofed?)
	+6 blessed boots of speed (rust proofed)
	+6 blessed helm of telepathy (rust proofed)
	blessed spellbook of magic mapping
	blessed spellbook of polymorph
	5 blessed wands of wishing
	blessed tinning kit

I had other stuff as well, but this is what I consider essential
to going after the Amulet.  Also, all my stats were maxed out,
and I had 350 to 400 hp's.

After I decided to go after the Amulet, it didn't take very long.
The hard part was being patient enough to equip myself properly
before heading out.

